    history:
      "The Orange River rises in highlands beyond South Africa's eastern border; its upper reach forms part of South Africa's border, and near its mouth at Alexander Bay it forms part of the country's north-western border — the river crosses several distinct landscape belts along its full course, but multiple sources agree it is South Africa's longest river. Augrabies Falls National Park has protected this distinctive granite gorge landscape since its establishment in 1966.",
